Usage: xftoxg [Options] input_file output_file
Options can be abbreviated, current short name abbreviations are in parentheses
Options:
 -input (-in)  OR  -InputFile   File
    Input file with f transforms
 -goutput (-g)  OR  -GOutputFile   File
    Output file for g transforms (optional if input name ends in xf)
 -nfit (-n)  OR  -NumberToFit   Int
    Number of adjacent sections to fit, 0 for global alignment, or 1 for fit
    to all sections
 -ref (-re)  OR  -ReferenceSection   Int
    Do a global alignment to the given section (numbered from 1)
 -order (-o)  OR  -OrderOfPolynomialFit   Int
    Order of the polynomial fit to the data. The default is 1 (linear fit).
 -mixed (-mi)  OR  -HybridFits   Int
    Number of parameters to eliminate trends for with a hybrid alignment
 -range (-ra)  OR  -RangeOfAnglesInAverage   Float
    Range of rotation angles for sections to include in average and fits
 -robust (-ro)  OR  -RobustFit
    Use robust weighting when fitting to find center position
 -kfactor (-k)  OR  -KFactorScaling   Int
    Amount to scale the K factor that controls how many points are
    down-weighted
 -max (-ma)  OR  -MaximumIterations   Int
    Maximum iterations in robust fitting (default 200, negative for trace)
 -iteration (-it)  OR  -IterationParams   3 floats
    Max fraction with zero weights, max change in weight without and with
    oscillations
 -help (-h)  OR  -usage
    Print help output
